 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Eleonora threatens to fire Mikhail Jekovich unless he restores order immediately, and sentences Senya and Fedya to work a week without pay and two weeks without days off. Mikhail immediately calls a buyer to get rid of the pony.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Быстро наведи в отеле порядок!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Иначе я тебя отсюда вышвырну.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "А вы двое слушайте меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Неделю работаете совсем без зарплаты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "И две недели без выходных.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Всё, быстро пошли вон отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Нет, это я не вам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Да, я срочно продаю пони.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Ещё как продаю, жду вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Айнура, быстро уберите всё здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "Я приехала работать в Москву.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "А теперь убираю за конём.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Быстро наведи в отеле порядок!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Quickly restore order in the hotel!' Pointing to the order to Mikhail, Eleonora chooses \"poryadok\" (\"order\") so Mikhail gets the point right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Иначе я тебя отсюда вышвырну.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Otherwise I will throw you out of here.' Eleonora proceeds bluntly on the spot, making her position completely clear.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "А вы двое слушайте меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And you two listen to me.' Eleonora counters bluntly without any doubt, shifting the mood of the conversation in a single beat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Неделю работаете совсем без зарплаты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will work a week with no salary at all.' Touching on the salaries right here, Eleonora lands on \"zarplaty\" (\"salaries\", built on \"zarplata\") to keep the statement grounded.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "И две недели без выходных.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And two weeks without days off.' Bringing up the weekend right here, Eleonora uses \"vykhodnykh\" (\"weekend\", from \"vykhodnoy\") to make the point stick.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Всё, быстро пошли вон отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is it, get out of here quickly!' Eleonora responds honestly beside Mikhail, bringing things back to earth after the buildup.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Нет, это я не вам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I did not mean that for you.' Mikhail answers decisively with a nod, watching Eleonora's face to see how the news lands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Да, я срочно продаю пони.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I am urgently selling a pony.' Emphasizing a pony around Eleonora, Mikhail leans on \"srochno\" (\"urgent, urgently\") to give the whole sentence its punch.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Ещё как продаю, жду вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I sure am selling it, I am waiting for you.' Mikhail speaks lightly without a pause, keeping the focus on what actually matters here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Айнура, быстро уберите всё здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Ainura, quickly clean everything up here.' Eleonora jumps in decisively right here and uses \"uberite\" (\"take away, remove\", from \"ubrat\") to make the point stick.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "Я приехала работать в Москву.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I came to work in Moscow.' Ainura responds boldly at once and chooses \"priyekhala\" (\"came, arrived\", from the root \"priyekhat\") so Eleonora hears the exact meaning.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "А теперь убираю за конём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
